BO_ 96 LAT_STOCK_TX_PAYLOAD_CANDIDATE: 9 BMW_I3
 SG_ LAT_STOCK_TX_PAYLOAD_BYTE_0 : 0|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ LAT_STOCK_TX_PAYLOAD_BYTE_1 : 8|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ LAT_STOCK_TX_PAYLOAD_BYTE_2 : 16|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ LAT_STOCK_TX_PAYLOAD_BYTE_3 : 24|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ LAT_STOCK_TX_PAYLOAD_BYTE_4 : 32|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
 SG_ LAT_STOCK_TX_PAYLOAD_BYTE_8 : 64|8@1+ (1,0) [0|255] "" BMW_I3
CM_ BO_ 96 "Primary lateral TX payload candidate. Routes 000000e9 and 000000ea provide the first labeled left/right windows; route 00000176 added dense managed-TJA coverage; route 00000402 (2026-03-27 TJA-only labeling pass) tightened the current practical decoder. Across all of them, src0/96 changes coherently during assisted-steering windows while src0/72 behaves like the outer TX phase/counter envelope. Current best practical decoder is phase-local on (72.byte0, 96.byte1), not a global scale in degrees. High-value phases where right means higher byte1 (R_high): phase 57 L/C/R ~ 63/174.5/236, phase 35 ~ 99/174.5/236, phase 49 ~ 81/175/217, phase 46 ~ 99/157/216. High-value phases where right means lower byte1 (R_low): phase 58 ~ 196.5/174.5/62, phase 25 ~ 176.5/110/62. Treat 96.byte2 as secondary torque/intensity-like support only. This frame remains the best current candidate for the actual stock lateral TX payload, but full command semantics are still unresolved.";
CM_ SG_ 96 LAT_STOCK_TX_PAYLOAD_BYTE_0 "Secondary phase/family byte inside the current best lateral TX payload frame. Useful for phase-local grouping together with frame 72 and byte1.";
CM_ SG_ 96 LAT_STOCK_TX_PAYLOAD_BYTE_1 "Best current direction-discriminating byte in the stock lateral TX payload. Decode only phase-locally with 72.byte0. Current strongest phases from route 00000402 are: R_high -> phase 57 (L/C/R ~ 63/174.5/236), phase 35 (99/174.5/236), phase 49 (81/175/217), phase 46 (99/157/216); R_low -> phase 58 (196.5/174.5/62), phase 25 (176.5/110/62). Do not treat byte1 as a global signed angle scale; the same numeric direction flips across phase families.";
CM_ SG_ 96 LAT_STOCK_TX_PAYLOAD_BYTE_2 "Auxiliary payload byte that moves with steering activity but is not yet isolated as a standalone signed magnitude. Relative to dynm/smnogar BMW SP2018 references, byte2 is the best current i3 candidate for a torque/intensity-like companion to byte1, but it is weaker than byte1 and should not be used as the primary direction discriminator.";
CM_ SG_ 96 LAT_STOCK_TX_PAYLOAD_BYTE_3 "Payload-support byte that remains structurally stable across many managed windows. Useful for identifying fixed-vs-dynamic portions of frame 96.";
CM_ SG_ 96 LAT_STOCK_TX_PAYLOAD_BYTE_4 "Payload-support byte that remains structurally stable across many managed windows. Useful for identifying fixed-vs-dynamic portions of frame 96.";
CM_ SG_ 96 LAT_STOCK_TX_PAYLOAD_BYTE_8 "Tail byte in the current best lateral TX payload frame. Keep as raw structural content until checksum/counter separation is proven.";

