CM_ BO_ 112 "Primary lateral RX/state helper. Confirmed on historical routes 00000054 and 00000055 and reinforced by managed-TJA route 00000176. Historical logs exposed it on src24; modern dual-FlexRay logging exposes the same frame on src1. It changes cleanly between manual driving, ACC-base, and TJA-assisted steering windows and is the best current candidate for reverse-engineering stock lateral control state/content. Byte5 bit5 is the strongest live discriminator: off/manual tends to set the bit, assisted steering tends to clear it. CarState now uses this as the live stock_lat_active_hint gate before trusting the phase-local 96 direction hint.";
CM_ SG_ 112 LAT_STOCK_MAIN_BYTE_5 "Best current live assisted-steering state discriminator. Bit5 set tends to mean manual/off; bit5 clear tends to mean assisted/TJA-active. CarState uses this to gate the phase-local 96 direction hint.";
CM_ SG_ 112 LAT_STOCK_ACTIVE_HINT "Derived boolean helper from LAT_STOCK_MAIN_BYTE_5 bit5. 1 means the stock lateral system appears active enough to trust 96 direction hints; 0 means suppress direction to unknown.";

