CM_ BO_ 217 "Confirmed PT-CAN accelerator-family frame. The first 16 bits remain useful as upstream positive/coast long-intent helper, while bytes 2:3 are now confirmed as the driver accelerator analog field on the i3. Current isolated pedal routes show 4096 at release and 8096 at full pedal, giving a clean 0..4000 working span after subtracting 4096.";
CM_ SG_ 217 ACCEL_RAW_PT_CAN "Best current upstream positive/coast long-intent candidate. Cross-route fit against longitudinalPlan.aTarget on 147/148/170/176/177 shows this raw 16-bit field correlates materially better with positive/coast intent than downstream 59/54 words. Current pragmatic managed-mode medians: POS ~63334, COAST ~63364.";
CM_ SG_ 217 ACCELERATOR_WORD23_PT_CAN "Confirmed raw accelerator word from bytes 2:3 on PT-CAN frame 217. Isolated pedal routes show release ~4096 and full pedal ~8096.";
CM_ SG_ 217 ACCELERATOR_VALUE_PT_CAN "Confirmed driver accelerator analog value on PT-CAN frame 217, derived as bytes2:3 minus 4096. Practical observed range: 0 release to 4000 full pedal.";
CM_ SG_ 217 ACCELERATOR_I4_COMPAT_PT_CAN "Legacy i4-compatible helper view of frame 217. Keep as comparison/support only; current i3 long fitting works better on the raw 16-bit field than on this compressed 12-bit projection.";

